================================================================================================================
  (e) On FRW the frozen phi leaves GR + BPS: FP7's marginal zero-field mode is gone (E1: PASS).  Where the web crosses the yield: onset exponent of the chord 0.5000-0.5000, tangent -0.5000--0.5000, at most 1 crossing per mode, the chord's step at a crossing shrinks x3.10-3.52 under 10x refinement
      (E2: FAIL -- on its absolute threshold only: the chord at d = 1.8e-13 y_th is 4.2e-04 = O(sqrt(d)/y_th) at y_th = 1e-6, not < 1e-5);
      sigma_8 converges monotonically as the yield is regularised (|d sigma_8| 2.5e-04/2.7e-05/2.6e-06 at eps/sqrt(y_th) = 0.1/0.01/0.001), d ln sigma_8/d ln A 0.9896 (eps = 0) vs 0.9894 (smooth); forest proxy at the three eps 3.8e-02/3.7e-03/3.7e-04 vs 2.8e-07 at eps = 0 (E3: FAIL -- on its forest tolerance 1e-6 only: the regularised plug leaks x ~ eps y/y_th below the yield, so the forest proxy converges linearly in eps);
      FP9's z ~ 2 lumps switch on once, continuously, and the tangent's divergence adds a finite number of Jeans e-folds (E4: PASS).
      No jump in G_eff and no instability at the crossing on the tested yardsticks.
